  <h1>Tapered Language Models: Free Perplexity via Layer-Aware Capacity</h1>
  <p class="lead">Every modern LM gives each layer the exact same MLP width — a default nobody questioned. Tapered LMs break this convention: taper MLP width monotonically from wide-early to narrow-late, keep the same total parameter budget, and gain −1.84 perplexity points for free. It works across Transformers, Gated Attention, Hope-attention, and Titans.</p>
