<p>Perplexity results are equally consistent: LAMBADA PPL improves in all 8 comparisons; WikiText in 7 of 8. The gains don't diminish at 1.3B — every architecture improves at both scales, suggesting depth-aware capacity allocation doesn't saturate. The core takeaway: <strong>tapering is a free architectural lever</strong>, hidden in plain sight since the original Transformer paper.</p>

